"""A mostly lexical detector of sources and provenance.

Predict a strong negative contribution for 'source', a smaller one for
'from', 'original', and source-code names. Chinese source words and two
other-language source stems behave similarly. 'Apart/away from' and
'open source' are weaker than the ordinary source/origin uses.
Spelling and attached punctuation change the predicted strength.
All other tokens return zero; earlier context beyond one token is ignored.
