It fires on the word "set" in the spellings a programmer or writer uses for it: "set",
"Set", "SET", "sets", and camelCase or underscore forms such as ".setItem", "setTitle",
"_set". On those tokens its activation is about 4. Weaker forms: "setter" about 3,
"setting" about 2, "setup" and "settings" about 1. Other words that merely contain "set"
(settle, subset, dataset) get a small value, about 0.7. Every other token gets 0.
